  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Find the largest area of a rectangle whose perimeter is 8 m.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4\\text{ m}^2$.",
      "worked": "Let the side lengths be $x$ m and $y$ m.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2y&=8\\\\y&=4-x.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $0<x<4$, the area is\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=xy\\\\A&=x(4-x).\\end{align*}$$\nThis downward-opening parabola has intercepts at $x=0$ and $x=4$, so its maximum occurs halfway between them.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{0+4}{2}=2\\\\y&=4-2=2\\\\A&=2(4-2)=4.\\end{align*}$$\nThe largest area is $4\\text{ m}^2$, achieved by a square with side length 2 m.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
